#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""turn-pause-lifecycle: run the turn-pause hook in one isolated, real session and check
that a paused turn can spend its grace, stop its own work, park and resume.

    turn-pause-lifecycle --harness claude-code|codex [--out DIR] [--model NAME]
    turn-pause-lifecycle observe EVENT        (the recording hook the driver wires)

Spec: docs/specs/2026-11-01-turn-pause-design.md ("Warning, pause, notification",
"Closing allowlist", "Resuming and granting more"); plan Task 9. It is a live
operation: each run spends model quota (cheap models, minimal prompts).

Isolation. The run directory (OUT, a new temporary directory by default) holds a
temporary HOME, XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, TMPDIR and harness
home (Claude Code: CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR plus `--settings`, with `--setting-sources project
--strict-mcp-config --disable-slash-commands`; Codex: CODEX_HOME). Every subprocess gets
an environment built key by key. PATH is OUT/bin (the harness, tasks, an `hq` that runs
this checkout's tools/hq, and a `notify-send` stub that only logs) then /usr/bin:/bin.
The hooks run this checkout's tools/turn-pause by explicit path with
--limits tools/fixtures/turn-pause/lifecycle/limits.toml (6 calls), next to a recording
hook (`observe`) that appends each payload to OUT/hooks.jsonl and never decides. A
throwaway tasks project (prefix tpl) lives in OUT/work, registered only under the
temporary XDG_CONFIG_HOME. Codex's auth.json is a symlink to the live login, never a
copy: before the run only its last_refresh is read (over 7 days refuses the run), and
after it the link is checked; a regular file Codex wrote in its place is copied over the
live file (mode 600) and reported. Every process the run starts carries a marker in its
environment and is reaped on exit, TERM and INT; Codex runs in a private tmux server
whose socket is under OUT, killed in a finally.

Stages, each asserted from the state snapshots (OUT/states.jsonl, polled while the
session runs, since SessionEnd removes the state file) and the transcripts:
  1 cross    the agent starts its background work, and its seventh root call is refused
             with the root refusal text (paused on calls, 7 of 6)
  2 grace    25 allowlisted reads pass after the pause; the next read is refused with
             the grace text
  3 cancel   the agent stops its own work: Claude Code loads TaskStop with ToolSearch
             select:TaskStop (not loaded before) and stops its background task, and
             kills its other process; Codex kills its process through a nested
             exec_command, interrupts its worker with interrupt_agent and sets its goal
             to paused; the processes are gone
  4 park     tasks park ... --waiting-on user succeeds and the turn ends (Codex: and no
             goal continuation turn follows within the watch window)
  5 resume   the genuine prompt `continue` in the same session ends the pause, resets
             the counters and runs one allowed shell command
The session runs in one process across the pause (Claude Code: stream-json input;
Codex: the interactive interface), so the pause still stands when `continue` arrives.

Prints one line per stage and PASS, or FAIL naming the failing stages; writes
OUT/summary.json with host paths replaced (<run> for OUT, ~ for the home directory).
"""
